== Effects ==
* Upon entering a {{R|Devil Room}}, a white inverted cross will appear above Isaac's head. If Isaac goes to the next floor with the icon still above his head, he will gain a {{e|Soul Heart}} and +1.0 [[damage]].
* Taking anything generated by the room (items or consumables) will result in the icon going away, including opening {{e|Red Chest}}s / {{e|Black Sack}}s.

== Notes ==
* After Isaac has taken a [[Devil Room#Deals with the Devil|Devil Deal]], while a {{M|Confessional}} would give an {{ip|Angel Room|text=Angel Room item}}, it has a 100% chance to spawn Redemption instead; while a {{R|Sacrifice Room}} would give a {{e|Soul Heart}}, it has a 50% chance to spawn Redemption instead. This is the only way Redemption can be naturally generated during a run, as the item is not in any [[item pool]].
** Other reliable ways include using {{i|Death Certificate}}, or using {{i|Spindown Dice}} on {{i|Spirit Shackles}}.
** Redemption has a small chance to be a starting item as {{c|Eden}}, {{c|Tainted Eden}}, or any character with {{i|Eden's Blessing}}.
** Using {{i|Birthright}} as {{c|Eden}} has a small chance to spawn Redemption.
** If {{i|Act of Contrition}} was taken after taking a Devil Deal, Redemption is not guaranteed to spawn.
* If there is an item in a {{e|Red Chest}}, the icon will not disappear, even if the item is taken.
* Opening {{e|Red Chest}}s that have been spawned after room generation, e.g. as a room clear reward or enemy drop, or opening them with {{i|Magneto}}, won't remove the icon.
* Taking {{i|A Lump of Coal}} or {{i|Head of Krampus}} after a {{E|Krampus}} fight will keep the icon.
* Picking up items made free through usage of items such as {{i|Coupon}} or a {{p|Credit Card}} will still remove the icon and provide no benefit.
** However, swapping out a free active item for another that was already held will not remove the icon.
* Taking free pickups/items that spawned after the room was entered (e. g. room clear rewards, drops from {{e|Fire Place}}s, rewards from {{m|Devil Beggar}}s) will not remove the cross.
* Taking pickups/items spawned by {{i|Keeper's Box}} inside the Devil Room will remove the cross.
* Taking items from a {{R|Black Market}} or {{I|A Pound of Flesh}} affected {{r|Shop}} will not remove the cross.

== Interactions ==
* {{t|Devil's Crown}}: Devil Treasure Rooms will count as regular {{r|Devil Room}}s for the purposes of this item.
* {{t|Found Soul}}: The soul will receive a cross when a Devil Room is entered, and will not lose it when Isaac takes an item/pickup. When Isaac goes to a new floor with the familiar having the cross, the soul will receive a damage boost (even if Isaac doesn't) and a Soul Heart, allowing it to survive multiple hits.
* {{C|Jacob and Esau}}: The cross will only disappear if the character holding Redemption takes something. The other character is free to take items and pickups.
* {{i|Satanic Bible}}: Taking a Boss item that was replaced with a Devil Deal will remove the cross, however the {{r|Boss Room}} doesn't give the cross.
* {{c|Tainted Lazarus}}: Only the character initially entering the {{r|Devil Room}} will receive the cross over his head. The character that leaves the floor with the icon above his head is the one that gains Redemption's benefits.
** Using {{i|Flip}} inside the Devil Room will make both forms have the icon over their heads. Even if one form's cross is removed, the other's is unaffected.
** Ghostly items that were already bought from taking a deal can safely be taken without deactivating Redemption.

